{"path":"3/library/reprlib.html","title":"reprlib — Alternate repr() implementation","description":"Source code: Lib/reprlib.py","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"module-reprlib"},{"type":"anchor","id":"reprlib-alternate-repr-implementation"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"reprlib"},{"type":"text","value":" — Alternate "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#repr","title":"repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" implementation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.14/Lib/reprlib.py","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lib/reprlib.py"}]}]},{"type":"thematic_break"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"reprlib"},{"type":"text","value":" module provides a means for producing object representations with limits on the size of the resulting strings. This is used in the Python debugger and may be useful in other contexts as well."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module provides a class, an instance, and a function:"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"reprlib.Repr("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"*"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxlevel"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxtuple"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxlist"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxarray"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"5"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxdict"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"4"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxset"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxfrozenset"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxdeque"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxstring"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"30"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxlong"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"40"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maxother"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"30"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fillvalue"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"'...'"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"indent"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Class which provides formatting services useful in implementing functions similar to the built-in "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#repr","title":"repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr()"}]},{"type":"text","value":"; size limits for different object types are added to avoid the generation of representations which are excessively long."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The keyword arguments of the constructor can be used as a shortcut to set the attributes of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Repr"},{"type":"text","value":" instance. Which means that the following initialization:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"aRepr = reprlib.Repr(maxlevel=3)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Is equivalent to:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"aRepr = reprlib.Repr()\naRepr.maxlevel = 3"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See section "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#id1","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr Objects"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more information about "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Repr"},{"type":"text","value":" attributes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.12: Allow attributes to be set via keyword arguments."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.aRepr","term":[{"type":"text","value":"reprlib.aRepr"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is an instance of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr","title":"reprlib.Repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Repr"}]},{"type":"text","value":" which is used to provide the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.repr","title":"reprlib.repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function described below. Changing the attributes of this object will affect the size limits used by "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr()"},{"type":"text","value":" and the Python debugger."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.repr","term":[{"type":"text","value":"reprlib.repr("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"obj"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr.repr","title":"reprlib.Repr.repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"aRepr"},{"type":"text","value":". It returns a string similar to that returned by the built-in function of the same name, but with limits on most sizes."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In addition to size-limiting tools, the module also provides a decorator for detecting recursive calls to "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__repr__","title":"object.__repr__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__repr__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and substituting a placeholder string instead."}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.recursive_repr","term":[{"type":"text","value":"@reprlib.recursive_repr("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fillvalue"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"'...'"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decorator for "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__repr__","title":"object.__repr__","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"__repr__()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" methods to detect recursive calls within the same thread. If a recursive call is made, the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fillvalue"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is returned, otherwise, the usual "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"__repr__()"},{"type":"text","value":" call is made. For example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"pycon","code":">>> from reprlib import recursive_repr\n>>> class MyList(list):\n...     @recursive_repr()\n...     def __repr__(self):\n...         return '<' + '|'.join(map(repr, self)) + '>'\n...\n>>> m = MyList('abc')\n>>> m.append(m)\n>>> m.append('x')\n>>> print(m)\n<'a'|'b'|'c'|...|'x'>"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.2."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"repr-objects"},{"type":"anchor","id":"id1"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr Objects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr","title":"reprlib.Repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Repr"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instances provide several attributes which can be used to provide size limits for the representations of different object types, and methods which format specific object types."}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.fillvalue","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.fillvalue"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This string is displayed for recursive references. It defaults to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"..."},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.11."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxlevel","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxlevel"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Depth limit on the creation of recursive representations. The default is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"6"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxdict","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxdict"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxlist","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxlist"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxtuple","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxtuple"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxset","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxset"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxfrozenset","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxfrozenset"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxdeque","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxdeque"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxarray","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxarray"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits on the number of entries represented for the named object type. The default is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"4"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr.maxdict","title":"reprlib.Repr.maxdict","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"maxdict"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"5"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr.maxarray","title":"reprlib.Repr.maxarray","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"maxarray"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"6"},{"type":"text","value":" for the others."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxlong","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxlong"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maximum number of characters in the representation for an integer. Digits are dropped from the middle. The default is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"40"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxstring","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxstring"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limit on the number of characters in the representation of the string. Note that the “normal” representation of the string is used as the character source: if escape sequences are needed in the representation, these may be mangled when the representation is shortened. The default is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"30"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.maxother","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.maxother"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This limit is used to control the size of object types for which no specific formatting method is available on the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr","title":"reprlib.Repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Repr"}]},{"type":"text","value":" object. It is applied in a similar manner as "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr.maxstring","title":"reprlib.Repr.maxstring","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"maxstring"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The default is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"20"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.indent","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.indent"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If this attribute is set to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"},{"type":"text","value":" (the default), the output is formatted with no line breaks or indentation, like the standard "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#repr","title":"repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr()"}]},{"type":"text","value":". For example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"pycon","code":">>> example = [\n...     1, 'spam', {'a': 2, 'b': 'spam eggs', 'c': {3: 4.5, 6: []}}, 'ham']\n>>> import reprlib\n>>> aRepr = reprlib.Repr()\n>>> print(aRepr.repr(example))\n[1, 'spam', {'a': 2, 'b': 'spam eggs', 'c': {3: 4.5, 6: []}}, 'ham']"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"indent"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to a string, each recursion level is placed on its own line, indented by that string:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"pycon","code":">>> aRepr.indent = '-->'\n>>> print(aRepr.repr(example))\n[\n-->1,\n-->'spam',\n-->{\n-->-->'a': 2,\n-->-->'b': 'spam eggs',\n-->-->'c': {\n-->-->-->3: 4.5,\n-->-->-->6: [],\n-->-->},\n-->},\n-->'ham',\n]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"indent"},{"type":"text","value":" to a positive integer value behaves as if it was set to a string with that number of spaces:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"pycon","code":">>> aRepr.indent = 4\n>>> print(aRepr.repr(example))\n[\n    1,\n    'spam',\n    {\n        'a': 2,\n        'b': 'spam eggs',\n        'c': {\n            3: 4.5,\n            6: [],\n        },\n    },\n    'ham',\n]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.12."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.repr","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.repr("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"obj"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The equivalent to the built-in "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#repr","title":"repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that uses the formatting imposed by the instance."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reprlib.Repr.repr1","term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.repr1("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"obj"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"level"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recursive implementation used by "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr.repr","title":"reprlib.Repr.repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr()"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This uses the type of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"obj"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to determine which formatting method to call, passing it "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"obj"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"level"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The type-specific methods should call "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr1()"},{"type":"text","value":" to perform recursive formatting, with "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"level - 1"},{"type":"text","value":" for the value of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"level"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in the recursive call."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"text","value":"Repr.repr_TYPE("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"obj"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"level"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Formatting methods for specific types are implemented as methods with a name based on the type name. In the method name, "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TYPE"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is replaced by "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'_'.join(type(obj).__name__.split())"},{"type":"text","value":". Dispatch to these methods is handled by "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr.repr1","title":"reprlib.Repr.repr1","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"repr1()"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Type-specific methods which need to recursively format a value should call "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"self.repr1(subobj, level - 1)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"subclassing-repr-objects"},{"type":"anchor","id":"subclassing-reprs"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subclassing Repr Objects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The use of dynamic dispatching by "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr.repr1","title":"reprlib.Repr.repr1","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Repr.repr1()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" allows subclasses of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/reprlib.html#reprlib.Repr","title":"reprlib.Repr","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Repr"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to add support for additional built-in object types or to modify the handling of types already supported. This example shows how special support for file objects could be added:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"import reprlib\nimport sys\n\nclass MyRepr(reprlib.Repr):\n\n    def repr_TextIOWrapper(self, obj, level):\n        if obj.name in {'<stdin>', '<stdout>', '<stderr>'}:\n            return obj.name\n        return repr(obj)\n\naRepr = MyRepr()\nprint(aRepr.repr(sys.stdin))         # prints '<stdin>'"},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":"<stdin>"}]}}
